Honest reading: plain `ruff check` with ruff 0.16.9's defaults is a much
broader net than the old compileall step (defaults include pyupgrade,
flake8-datetime, blind-except, bandit-lite, isort, etc.). The codebase
does NOT pass it today. The CI lint job will therefore FAIL on the first
GitHub-hosted run until either (a) the code is cleaned to pass bare
`ruff check` — 318 findings, mostly style, 28 auto-fixable, none of them
bugs (compileall-equivalent syntax level is clean), or (b) the workflow
narrows the lint gate to an agreed rule set (e.g. --select E,F) with a
documented justification. That decision belongs to the team/parent —
this agent was told to use bare `ruff check` and did, and must not edit
code or tests itself.

